g alt="Increase" resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> £1,304.6<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>million (2025)<sup about="#mwt22" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-annual_2-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"annual"}}'><a href="#cite_note-annual-2" id="mwGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label"><div style="display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0; ">Number of employees</div></th><td class="infobox-data">12,200 (2025)<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-annual_2-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"annual"}}'><a href="#cite_note-annual-2" id="mwHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label">Website</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.revolut.com/" class="external text">www<wbr/>.revolut<wbr/>.com</a></span></td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwIA"><b id="mwIQ">Revolut Group Holdings Ltd</b>, known as <b id="mwIg">Revolut</b>,<sup about="#mwt28" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">]</span></span></a></sup> is a British global <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_technology" title="Financial technology" id="mwJw">financial technology</a> company headquartered in London and founded in July 2015 by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nik_Storonskiy" title="Nik Storonskiy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwKA">Nik Storonskiy</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vlad_Yatsenko" title="Vlad Yatsenko" id="mwKQ">Vlad Yatsenko</a>.<sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwKg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ">]</span></span></a></sup> As of March 2026, Revolut has over 70 million customers and supports transfers to more than 160 countries and regions.<sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-6" id="mwMg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNQ">]</span></span></a></sup> It was valued at $75 billion in November 2025.<sup about="#mwt40" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwNg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwOg">The company offers free and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subscription_business_model" title="Subscription business model" id="mwOw">subscription‑based</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_banking" title="Digital banking" id="mwPA">digital banking</a> services, primarily through a mobile app.<sup about="#mwt43" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mwPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt46" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-9" id="mwQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRA">]</span></span></a></sup> Its banking services include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_account" title="Bank account" id="mwRQ">bank accounts</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debit_card" title="Debit card" id="mwRg">debit cards</a>, credit cards, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Currency_exchange" title="Currency exchange" class="mw-redirect" id="mwRw">currency exchange</a> in over 25 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiat_currencies" title="Fiat currencies" class="mw-redirect" id="mwSA">fiat currencies</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stock_trading" title="Stock trading" class="mw-redirect" id="mwSQ">stock trading</a>, cryptocurrency exchange, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peer-to-peer" title="Peer-to-peer" id="mwSg">peer-to-peer</a> payments.<sup about="#mwt49" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-techcrunch1_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"techcrunch1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-techcrunch1-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-techcrunch1-10" id="mwSw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTQ">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTg">]</span></span></a></sup> For businesses, the Revolut Business platform provides multi‑currency corporate accounts, payroll processing, and integration with accounting software.<sup about="#mwt52" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwTw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUQ">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUg">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile_app" title="Mobile app" id="mwUw">mobile app</a> supports spending and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_teller_machine" title="Automated teller machine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwVA">ATM</a> withdrawals in 120 currencies and transfers in 36 currencies.<sup about="#mwt55" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-12" id="mwVQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt58" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TechCrunch_2018-05-24_13-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TechCrunch 2018-05-24"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TechCrunch_2018-05-24-13"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TechCrunch_2018-05-24-13" id="mwWQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut's credit card is available in Poland, Lithuania, the United States, and Ireland.<sup about="#mwt61" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-monito_20230323_14-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"monito_20230323"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-monito_20230323-14"}}'><a href="#cite_note-monito_20230323-14" id="mwXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXw">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwYQ" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwYg" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwYw" aria-labelledby="Early_history_(2015–2017)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Early_history_(2015–2017)"><span id="Early_history_.282015.E2.80.932017.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Early history (2015–2017)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Early history (2015–2017)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwZA">Revolut was founded in 2015 by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nik_Storonsky" title="Nik Storonsky" id="mwZQ">Nik Storonsky</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vlad_Yatsenko" title="Vlad Yatsenko" id="mwZg">Vlad Yatsenko</a> as an app enabling individuals in the United Kingdom and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Economic_Area" title="European Economic Area" id="mwZw">European Economic Area (EEA)</a> to spend money abroad using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interbank_foreign_exchange_market" title="Interbank foreign exchange market" id="mwaA">interbank foreign exchange</a> rates.<sup about="#mwt64" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CE_15-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CE"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CE-15"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CE-15" id="mwaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt67" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-founded_16-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"founded"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-founded-16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-founded-16" id="mwbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcA">]</span></span></a></sup> Customers could use their Revolut card in 90 currencies.<sup about="#mwt68" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CE_15-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CE"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CE-15" id="mwcQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt71" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-17" id="mwdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mweA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mweQ">In 2016, the company reached around 300,000 users, processing almost £1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mweg"> </span>billion in transactions.<sup about="#mwt74" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-forbes_20160725_popular_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"forbes_20160725_popular"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-forbes_20160725_popular-18"}}'><a href="#cite_note-forbes_20160725_popular-18" id="mwew"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfQ">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwfw">Revolut then launched a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subscription_business_model" title="Subscription business model" id="mwgA">subscription-based</a> app in June 2017 available to businesses across the UK and Europe. Under the name of "Revolut Business", businesses could create an account with a multi-currency <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBAN" title="IBAN" class="mw-redirect" id="mwgQ">IBAN</a> to hold, exchange, and transfer money with 25 currencies.<sup about="#mwt77" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-19" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-19"}}'><a href="#cite_note-19" id="mwgg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhA">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt80" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-techcrunch_20170613_revolut_20-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"techcrunch_20170613_revolut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-techcrunch_20170613_revolut-20"}}'><a href="#cite_note-techcrunch_20170613_revolut-20" id="mwhg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiA">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwig" aria-labelledby="EU_banking_licence_and_international_expansion_(2017–2022)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="EU_banking_licence_and_international_expansion_(2017–2022)"><span id="EU_banking_licence_and_international_expansion_.282017.E2.80.932022.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>EU banking licence and international expansion (2017–2022)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: EU banking licence and international expansion (2017–2022)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwiw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Vilnius_Quadrum.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwjA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Vilnius_Quadrum.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/Vilnius_Quadrum.jpg/250px-Vilnius_Quadrum.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4284" data-file-height="2908" data-file-type="bitmap" height="170" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/Vilnius_Quadrum.jpg/500px-Vilnius_Quadrum.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwjQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwjg">Quadrum office complex in Vilnius, head office of Revolut Bank UAB (name visible on left)</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwjw">It first applied for an EU banking licence in November 2017, at which time it also started work on its own <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Payment_processor" title="Payment processor" id="mwkA">payment processor</a>.<sup about="#mwt83" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-independent_8043306_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"independent_8043306"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-independent_8043306-21"}}'><a href="#cite_note-independent_8043306-21" id="mwkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt86" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-22" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-22"}}'><a href="#cite_note-22" id="mwlQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlw">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmA">]</span></span></a></sup> The bank then received its EU banking licence as well as an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_Money_Institution" title="Electronic Money Institution" id="mwmQ">EMI</a> licence in December 2018 from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Central_Bank" title="European Central Bank" id="mwmg">European Central Bank</a>, facilitated by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_of_Lithuania" title="Bank of Lithuania" id="mwmw">Bank of Lithuania</a>. Under its new license, the bank could accept deposits and offer consumer credits, but it was not allowed to provide investment services until later.<sup about="#mwt89" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-23" id="mwnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwng">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt92" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ft_989904_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ft_989904"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ft_989904-24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ft_989904-24" id="mwoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwog">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwow">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt95" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cnbc_20181213_revolut_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cnbc_20181213_revolut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-cnbc_20181213_revolut-25"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cnbc_20181213_revolut-25" id="mwpA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwpQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpg">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwqA">Following the acquisition of a banking licence, the company announced plans in September 2019 for expansion into 24 new markets, supported by agreements with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visa_Inc." title="Visa Inc." id="mwqQ">Visa</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mastercard" title="Mastercard" id="mwqg">Mastercard</a>. The company said that it also wanted to hire an additional 3,500 employees.<sup about="#mwt98" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26"}}'><a href="#cite_note-26" id="mwqw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrQ">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-27" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-27"}}'><a href="#cite_note-27" id="mwrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwsA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsQ">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt104" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-28" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-28"}}'><a href="#cite_note-28" id="mwsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtQ">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2019, the Revolut app launched in beta to the Australia region.<sup about="#mwt107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-techcrunch_20190612_revolut_29-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"techcrunch_20190612_revolut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-techcrunch_20190612_revolut-29"}}'><a href="#cite_note-techcrunch_20190612_revolut-29" id="mwtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuQ">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwug">]</span></span></a></sup> The following month, Revolut expanded to Singapore.<sup about="#mwt110" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-techcrunch_20191023_revolut_30-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"techcrunch_20191023_revolut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-techcrunch_20191023_revolut-30"}}'><a href="#cite_note-techcrunch_20191023_revolut-30" id="mwuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvQ">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2020, the app launched in the United States and Japan.<sup about="#mwt113" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mwvw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwQ">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt116" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mwww"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxQ">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwxw">By November 2020, Revolut reported that it had reached breakeven. At that time, it was valued at £4.2 billion.<sup about="#mwt119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-33" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-33" id="mwyA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwzA">The company applied for banking licence in the United Kingdom and a bank charter in the United States in early 2021.<sup about="#mwt122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mwzQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzw">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-35" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-35" id="mw0Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0w">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt128" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-dillet_36-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"dillet"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-dillet-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-dillet-36" id="mw1Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1w">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2A">]</span></span></a></sup> The European Central Bank also granted Revolut a full banking licence later that year.<sup about="#mwt131" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-37" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-37" id="mw2Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2w">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mw3Q" aria-labelledby="Transition_to_a_licensed_bank_(2022–2023)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Transition_to_a_licensed_bank_(2022–2023)"><span id="Transition_to_a_licensed_bank_.282022.E2.80.932023.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Transition to a licensed bank (2022–2023)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Transition to a licensed bank (2022–2023)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw3g">After having secured bank licences, Revolut started moving away from being an e-money institution to a bank. In January 2022, it started operating as a bank in 10 European countries.<sup about="#mwt134" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mw3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4Q">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4g">]</span></span></a></sup> In January 2023, the company announced that it would transfer its 2 million Irish customers to a new Irish branch, moving them from a Lithuanian <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBAN" title="IBAN" class="mw-redirect" id="mw4w">IBAN</a> to an Irish IBAN.<sup about="#mwt137" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-independent_42306631_39-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"independent_42306631"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-independent_42306631-39"}}'><a href="#cite_note-independent_42306631-39" id="mw5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5g">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5w">]</span></span></a></sup> This was followed by a launch for IBANs in France, Netherlands and Spain in September 2023.<sup about="#mwt140" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-40" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-40"}}'><a href="#cite_note-40" id="mw6A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6g">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Financial_Times_41-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Financial Times"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Financial_Times-41"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Financial_Times-41" id="mw7A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7g">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7w">]</span></span></a></sup> By the end of the year, it was reported that Revolut held £15.1 billion in customer deposits.<sup about="#mwt146" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bbc_57854969_42-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bbc_57854969"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bbc_57854969-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bbc_57854969-42" id="mw8A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-$33_billion_43-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"$33 billion"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-$33_billion-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-$33_billion-43" id="mw9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9g">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mw-A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw-Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-g">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-w">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mw_A">Revolut expanded its investment offerings during this time. In September 2022, the UK's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Conduct_Authority" title="Financial Conduct Authority" id="mw_Q">Financial Conduct Authority</a> added Revolut to its list of companies authorised to offer cryptocurrency products and services, formalising its pre-2022 unregulated crypto trading.<sup about="#mwt155" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mw_g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw_w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQA">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQE">]</span></span></a></sup> The bank also began allowing staking for holders of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proof_of_stake" title="Proof of stake" id="mwAQI">proof of stake</a> cryptocurrencies in the UK and EEA.<sup about="#mwt156" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Financial_Times_41-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Financial Times"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Financial_Times-41" id="mwAQM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQU">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt159" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAQc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQk">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQo">]</span></span></a></sup> In October 2023, Revolut expanded its stock trading services to include European stock trading in the EEA.<sup about="#mwt162" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwAQs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ0">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt165" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARE">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt168" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwARM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARU">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwARc">In September 2022, Revolut was the target of a cyber attack that exposed the personal data of over 50,000 customers.<sup about="#mwt171" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-techcrunch_20220920_revolut_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"techcrunch_20220920_revolut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-techcrunch_20220920_revolut-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-techcrunch_20220920_revolut-50" id="mwARg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARo">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt174" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwARw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAR0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR4">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR8">]</span></span></a></sup> Additionally, in July 2023, a flaw in its US payment system led to the loss of $20 million in corporate funds to criminal groups between late 2021 and early 2022, though some of the money was later recouped.<sup about="#mwt177" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AT_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AT"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AT-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AT-52" id="mwASA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASI">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASM">]</span></span></a></sup> On the regulatory front, Revolut halted <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptocurrency" title="Cryptocurrency" id="mwASQ">cryptocurrency</a> trading services for its US customers in 2023, citing the "evolving regulatory environment" as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Securities_and_Exchange_Commission" title="United States Securities and Exchange Commission" id="mwASU">Securities and Exchange Commission</a> intensified scrutiny against the sector.<sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-53" id="mwASY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASg">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASk">]</span></span></a></sup> Financially, despite its growth, the company reported £25m loss in 2022 amid ongoing uncertainty regarding the UK banking licence.<sup about="#mwt183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwASo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASw">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwAS4" aria-labelledby="UK_banking_licence_and_global_expansion_(2024–2026)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="UK_banking_licence_and_global_expansion_(2024–2026)"><span id="UK_banking_licence_and_global_expansion_.282024.E2.80.932026.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>UK banking licence and global expansion (2024–2026)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: UK banking licence and global expansion (2024–2026)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAS8">By August 2024, the company had doubled its headcount over the past two years, employing over 8,000 people in more than 25 countries.<sup about="#mwt186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwATA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATI">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATM">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut was also granted a British banking licence the following month, though with restrictions via the standard "mobilization" stage.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwATQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATY">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATc">]</span></span></a></sup> By the end of 2024, Revolut reported having 50 million registered users globally.<sup about="#mwt192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwATg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATs">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwATw">In April 2025, Revolut obtained the Prepaid Payment Instruments (PPIs) licence from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reserve_Bank_of_India" title="Reserve Bank of India" id="mwAT0">Reserve Bank of India</a> (RBI), to offer payment solutions including pre-paid cards.<sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-indiatimes_120044076_58-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"indiatimes_120044076"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-indiatimes_120044076-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-indiatimes_120044076-58" id="mwAT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUA">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAUI">In May 2025, Revolut announced that it plans to invest $1.1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAUM"> </span>billion over the next three years to expand in France and made Paris its Western European headquarters, at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choose_France?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Choose France (page does not exist)" about="#mwt196" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:LocalizedAttrs" class="new" id="mwAUQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Interlanguage link","href":"./Template:Interlanguage_link"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Choose France"},"2":{"wt":"fr"}},"i":0}}]}' data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Choose France"]}}'>Choose France</a><span class="noprint" style="font-size:85%; font-style: normal; " about="#mwt196" id="mwAUU"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choose%20France" title="fr:Choose France" class="extiw">fr</a><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></span> summit.<sup about="#mwt199" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-co_20250519_revolut_59-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"co_20250519_revolut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-co_20250519_revolut-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-co_20250519_revolut-59" id="mwAUY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUg">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt202" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwAUo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUw">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>  

<p id="mwAU4">In June 2025, Revolut announced its plans to acquire <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetelem_Argentina?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Cetelem Argentina (page does not exist)" about="#mwt203" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:LocalizedAttrs" class="new" id="mwAU8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Interlanguage link","href":"./Template:Interlanguage_link"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Cetelem Argentina"},"2":{"wt":"es"}},"i":0}}]}' data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Cetelem Argentina"]}}'>Cetelem Argentina</a><span class="noprint" style="font-size:85%; font-style: normal; " about="#mwt203" id="mwAVA"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetelem%20Argentina" title="es:Cetelem Argentina" class="extiw">es</a><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></span>, an Argentina-based lender, from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BNP_Paribas" title="BNP Paribas" id="mwAVE">BNP Paribas</a>. Terms were not disclosed.<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwAVI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVQ">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVU">]</span></span></a></sup> The same month, Béatrice Cossa-Dumurgier (a former board member of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Société_Générale" title="Société Générale" id="mwAVY">Société Générale</a> and executive at BNP Paribas) was appointed CEO of Revolut's Western Europe headquarters, based in Paris.<sup about="#mwt209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwAVc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVk">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVo">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2025, it named former <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Société_Générale" title="Société Générale" id="mwAVs">Société Générale</a> CEO <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frédéric_Oudéa" title="Frédéric Oudéa" id="mwAVw">Frédéric Oudéa</a> as Chairman of its Western Europe hub.<sup about="#mwt212" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwAV0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAV4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAV8">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWA">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAWE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Estacion_de_Aeropuerto_T1-T2-T3,_2025_(04).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAWI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Estacion_de_Aeropuerto_T1-T2-T3,_2025_(04).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Estacion_de_Aeropuerto_T1-T2-T3%2C_2025_%2804%29.jpg/250px-Estacion_de_Aeropuerto_T1-T2-T3%2C_2025_%2804%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="4640" data-file-height="6960" data-file-type="bitmap" height="375" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Estacion_de_Aeropuerto_T1-T2-T3%2C_2025_%2804%29.jpg/500px-Estacion_de_Aeropuerto_T1-T2-T3%2C_2025_%2804%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAWM"/></a><figcaption id="mwAWQ">Revolut ATM at Madrid Barajas Airport metro station</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwAWU">In summer 2025, Revolut launched first 50 own branded ATMs in Spain.<sup about="#mwt215" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwAWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWg">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWk">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, Revolut entered discussions with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_of_Israel" title="Bank of Israel" id="mwAWo">Bank of Israel</a> to obtain a "lean bank" licence.<sup about="#mwt218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-65"}}'><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwAWs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW0">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW4">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2025, Revolut secured in-principle approval for payments licence from the UAE.<sup about="#mwt221" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-66" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-66" id="mwAW8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXE">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXI">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2025, Revolut entered talks with Blackstone that could see the world's largest alternative-asset manager offering its funds on the Revolut platform.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwAXM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXU">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwAXc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXk">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXo">]</span></span></a></sup> In January 2026, Revolut applied for a full banking license in Peru as it sought to expand into Latin America. This marked the firm's fifth market expansion.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX0">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAX8">On 27 January 2026, Revolut launched full banking operations in Mexico. This marked Revolut's first bank established outside of Europe and become the first independent digital bank to secure a Mexican banking license through a direct application. Revolut capitalized its operations with over $100 million, which was more than double the regulatory minimum.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-70" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-70"}}'><a href="#cite_note-70" id="mwAYA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYI">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAYQ">On 11 March 2026, Revolut announced that they have received their <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banking_license" title="Banking license" id="mwAYU">full UK banking license</a>, which means that customers will now be protected by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Services_Compensation_Scheme" title="Financial Services Compensation Scheme" id="mwAYY">Financial Services Compensation Scheme</a> on any deposits under £120,000.<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-71" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-71"}}'><a href="#cite_note-71" id="mwAYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYk">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72"}}'><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwAYs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY0">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY4">]</span></span></a></sup> The licence also authorises the company to provide consumer credit services to UK customers.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-73" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-73"}}'><a href="#cite_note-73" id="mwAY8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZE">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAZM">In 2026, Revolut began offering a beta version of its services in India.<sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-74" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-74"}}'><a href="#cite_note-74" id="mwAZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZY">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwAZg" aria-labelledby="US_expansion_(2025–2026)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="US_expansion_(2025–2026)"><span id="US_expansion_.282025.E2.80.932026.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>US expansion (2025–2026)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: US expansion (2025–2026)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAZk">In 2025, Revolut explored an existing US bank acquisition to further expand its global footprint.<sup about="#mwt248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-75" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-75"}}'><a href="#cite_note-75" id="mwAZo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZw">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ0">]</span></span></a></sup> In February 2026, the company announced that it was shifting its plan to establish an independent national charter and had applied for a license with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_of_the_Comptroller_of_the_Currency" title="Office of the Comptroller of the Currency" id="mwAZ4">Office of the Comptroller of the Currency</a> (OCC).<sup about="#mwt251" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-76" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-76"}}'><a href="#cite_note-76" id="mwAZ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaE">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt252" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ref1_77-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ref1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ref1-77" id="mwAaM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaU">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAac">On 5 March 2026, Revolut announced it had applied for a US banking license with the OCC and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Deposit_Insurance_Corporation" title="Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation" id="mwAag">FDIC</a>.<sup about="#mwt255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-78"}}'><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwAak"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAao"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAas">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ref1_77-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ref1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ref1-77"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ref1-77" id="mwAa0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAa4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa8">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAbE">In an 20 April 2026 interview to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomberg_News" title="Bloomberg News" id="mwAbI">Bloomberg</a>, Revolut CEO <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nik_Storonsky" title="Nik Storonsky" id="mwAbM">Nik Storonsky</a> stated that the digital bank is approximately two years away from an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Initial_public_offering" title="Initial public offering" id="mwAbQ">IPO</a>, with a U.S. listing as the preference.<sup about="#mwt261" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}'><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAbU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbc">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbg">]</span></span></a></sup> The following day, the <i id="mwAbk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Times" title="Financial Times" id="mwAbo">Financial Times</a></i> reported that Revolut was targeting a market capitalisation of between $150 billion and $200 billion in its eventual IPO, and planned a secondary share sale in the second half of 2026 at a valuation exceeding $100 billion.<sup about="#mwt264" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-tc_ipo_2026_80-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"tc_ipo_2026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-tc_ipo_2026-80"}}'><a href="#cite_note-tc_ipo_2026-80" id="mwAbs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb0">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb4">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut reported revenue of $6 billion for the financial year ended 31 December 2025, up from $4 billion in 2024, and net profit of $1.7 billion, up from $1 billion, with 68.3 million retail customers at year-end.<sup about="#mwt265" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-tc_ipo_2026_80-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"tc_ipo_2026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-tc_ipo_2026-80" id="mwAb8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcE">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAcM" aria-labelledby="Products_and_services"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Products_and_services">Products and services</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Products and services"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAcQ">Revolut began as a mobile app linked to a prepaid card for spending abroad and foreign exchange. In 2016, <i id="mwAcU">The Guardian</i> described the service as allowing customers to spend in more than 90 currencies using an app-linked card.<sup about="#mwt268" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GuardianFX2016_81-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GuardianFX2016"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-GuardianFX2016-81"}}'><a href="#cite_note-GuardianFX2016-81" id="mwAcY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcg">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAck">]</span></span></a></sup> The company later expanded into banking, business accounts, lending, subscriptions, investments and cryptocurrency services.<sup about="#mwt271" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReutersProfit2025_82-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReutersProfit2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReutersProfit2025-82"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReutersProfit2025-82" id="mwAco"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcw">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt274" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReutersProfit20262_83-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReutersProfit20262"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReutersProfit20262-83"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReutersProfit20262-83" id="mwAc4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdA">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdE">]</span></span></a></sup> Product availability vary by country.<sup about="#mwt277" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-RevolutCompanies_84-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"RevolutCompanies"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-RevolutCompanies-84"}}'><a href="#cite_note-RevolutCompanies-84" id="mwAdI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdQ">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdU">]</span></span></a></sup> After Revolut received its full UK banking licence, Reuters reported that the company planned to introduce credit cards, unsecured personal loans and overdrafts in the UK.<sup about="#mwt280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReutersProfit2026_85-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReutersProfit2026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReutersProfit2026-85"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReutersProfit2026-85" id="mwAdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdg">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwAdo" aria-labelledby="Foreign_exchange_and_transfers"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Foreign_exchange_and_transfers">Foreign exchange and transfers</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Foreign exchange and transfers"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAds">Foreign exchange, international payments and multi-currency are central parts of Revolut's service.<sup about="#mwt283" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-86"}}'><a href="#cite_note-86" id="mwAdw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAd0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd4">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd8">]</span></span></a></sup> Reuters has described Revolut's business model as relying heavily on payments and foreign exchange activity, with lending remaining a smaller part of the company after it received its UK banking licence.<sup about="#mwt286" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-87" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-87"}}'><a href="#cite_note-87" id="mwAeA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeI">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwAeQ" aria-labelledby="Subscription_plans"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Subscription_plans">Subscription plans</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Subscription plans"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAeU">Revolut has a tiered consumer subscription model. <i id="mwAeY">Forbes Advisor</i> lists five UK personal accounts: Standard, Plus, Premium, Metal and Ultra, with Standard offered without a monthly fee and the other plans with a monthly cost.<sup about="#mwt289" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ForbesRevolutReview2026_88-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ForbesRevolutReview2026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ForbesRevolutReview2026-88"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ForbesRevolutReview2026-88" id="mwAec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeo">]</span></span></a></sup> The paid tiers differ by account allowances and included services, including ATM withdrawal limits, foreign spending, airport lounge access, cashback, insurance and investment-related features.<sup about="#mwt290" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ForbesRevolutReview2026_88-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ForbesRevolutReview2026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ForbesRevolutReview2026-88" id="mwAes"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAew"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe0">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwAe8" aria-labelledby="Investments_and_crypto"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Investments_and_crypto">Investments and crypto</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Investments and crypto"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAfA">Revolut expanded into investing in 2019 and launched in-app share trading for European customers. <i id="mwAfE">Wired</i> reported that the service allowed trading in 300 US-listed stocks on the New York Stock Exchange and Nasdaq.<sup about="#mwt293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WiredTrading2019_89-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WiredTrading2019"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WiredTrading2019-89"}}'><a href="#cite_note-WiredTrading2019-89" id="mwAfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfQ">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfU">]</span></span></a></sup> After receiving a UK trading licence in 2024, Revolut expanded its investment offering to include UK and EU-listed stocks and ETFs, and later launched a UK stocks and shares ISA using ETFs from providers including BlackRock and Vanguard.<sup about="#mwt296" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-90" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-90"}}'><a href="#cite_note-90" id="mwAfY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfg">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt299" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-91" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-91"}}'><a href="#cite_note-91" id="mwAfo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfw">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAf4" aria-labelledby="Revolut_Business"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Revolut_Business">Revolut Business</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Revolut Business"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwAf8">Revolut Business is a platform designed for business customers. It provides multi-currency accounts, payments, expense management, company cards and payment acceptance for businesses. In 2020, Revolut Business launched "merchant acquiring" i.e. accepting debit and credit card payments for its customers.<sup about="#mwt302" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-92" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-92"}}'><a href="#cite_note-92" id="mwAgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgI">[</span>92<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAgQ">As of 2025, the company had secured over 750,000 business customers.<sup about="#mwt305" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-93" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-93"}}'><a href="#cite_note-93" id="mwAgU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgc">[</span>93<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgg">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut Business also received awards for 'Best Mobile Banking App' by Global Finance<sup about="#mwt308" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-94" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-94"}}'><a href="#cite_note-94" id="mwAgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgs">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgw">]</span></span></a></sup> and 'Best Digital SME Bank' in Europe by The Digital Banker.<sup about="#mwt311" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-95" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-95"}}'><a href="#cite_note-95" id="mwAg0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAg4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg8">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwAhE" aria-labelledby="Criticism_and_controversies"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Criticism_and_controversies">Criticism and controversies</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Criticism and controversies"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAhI">Revolut has been subject to criticism and many controversies, such as issues with customer support and long-lasting lockouts,<sup about="#mwt314" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-96" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-96"}}'><a href="#cite_note-96" id="mwAhM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhU">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhY">]</span></span></a></sup> as well as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti–money_laundering" title="Anti–money laundering" id="mwAhc">anti–money laundering</a> compliance failures<sup about="#mwt317" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-97" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-97"}}'><a href="#cite_note-97" id="mwAhg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAho">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhs">]</span></span></a></sup> and lack of support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defrauder" title="Defrauder" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhw">defrauded</a> customers.<sup about="#mwt320" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-theguardian_2024apr10_im_98-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"theguardian_2024apr10_im"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-theguardian_2024apr10_im-98"}}'><a href="#cite_note-theguardian_2024apr10_im-98" id="mwAh0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAh4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh8">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt323" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-99" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-99"}}'><a href="#cite_note-99" id="mwAiE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiM">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiQ">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the company has since reported improvements to its customer service. In 2025, average resolution times decreased by over 40% for retail support and by more than 50% for business support.<sup about="#mwt326" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-100" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-100"}}'><a href="#cite_note-100" id="mwAiU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAic">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAig">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwAik" aria-labelledby="Employment_practices"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Employment_practices">Employment practices</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Employment practices"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAio">In March 2019, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wired_(magazine)" title="Wired (magazine)" id="mwAis"><i id="mwAiw">Wired</i></a> published an exposé of the company's employment practices and work culture. It included allegations by some former employees of unpaid work, high staff turnover, and employees feeling the need to work weekends to meet <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Performance_indicator" title="Performance indicator" id="mwAi0">performance indicators</a>.<sup about="#mwt329" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-101" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-101"}}'><a href="#cite_note-101" id="mwAi4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAi8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjA">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjE">]</span></span></a></sup> A later article in December 2019 by <i id="mwAjI">Sifted</i> noted that Revolut had a higher rating on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glassdoor" title="Glassdoor" id="mwAjM">Glassdoor</a> than its peers.<sup about="#mwt332" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-102" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-102"}}'><a href="#cite_note-102" id="mwAjQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjY">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwAjg" aria-labelledby="Inadequate_compliance"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Inadequate_compliance">Inadequate compliance</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Inadequate compliance"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwAjk">In 2016, a former employee approached UK's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Conduct_Authority" title="Financial Conduct Authority" id="mwAjo">Financial Conduct Authority</a> with claims regarding Revolut's leadership conduct and compliance practices. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whistleblower" title="Whistleblower" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAjs">whistleblower</a> emphasized that the company's anti-money laundering systems were utterly inadequate and that  money-laundering checks were not being properly applied for select customers. Numerous Revolut's employees contacted by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC" title="BBC" id="mwAjw">BBC</a> corroborated the whistleblower's testimony and also confirmed that Revolut's CEO allegedly ignored recommendations from its compliance team and conflicted with compliance executives. One such internal conflict led to departure of two chief risk officers, two money laundering reporting officers, a chief compliance officer, and  a chief finance officer, among other roles, within three years.<sup about="#mwt335" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bbccompliance_103-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bbccompliance"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bbccompliance-103"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bbccompliance-103" id="mwAj0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAj4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj8">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAkE">In 2018, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Daily_Telegraph" title="The Daily Telegraph" id="mwAkI">The Telegraph</a> reported that in the Summer 2018 Revolut disabled its system designed to automatically halt transactions to sanctioned individuals. In a draft letter to FCA, which was leaked to journalists, Revolut's lawyers confirmed that the internal system was changed so the transactions that potentially matched against sanctions lists were not halted, but rather flagged for inspections. The industry expert commenting on the case for BBC report emphasized that failing to halt transactions is by far the most serious compliance failure, as checking afterwards won't prevent state-level criminals from receiving the funds.<sup about="#mwt336" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bbccompliance_103-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bbccompliance"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bbccompliance-103" id="mwAkM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkU">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAkc">In July 2025, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Central_Bank" title="European Central Bank" id="mwAkg">European Central Bank</a> restricted Revolut's European arm's business activities due to deficiencies in the company's approval processes. ECB ordered Revolut to commission an independent risk review and  review staffing levels, expertise and independence within its product approval process.<sup about="#mwt339" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-104" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-104"}}'><a href="#cite_note-104" id="mwAkk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAko"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAks">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkw">]</span></span></a></sup> Such regulatory measures limited the bank's ability to launch new products. As of June 2026, it was unclear if bank followed the ECB's ruling and the restrictions were lifted.<sup about="#mwt342" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-105" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-105"}}'><a href="#cite_note-105" id="mwAk0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAk4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk8">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAlE">On a different occasion, Revolut was blamed for overcompliance, as it froze accounts of its customers with Russian passports and legal residence in Europe in 2025.<sup about="#mwt345" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-106" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-106"}}'><a href="#cite_note-106" id="mwAlI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlQ">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlU">]</span></span></a></sup> Storonsky blamed regulatory pressure. However, legal experts agreed that EU sanctions don't prohibit servicing European residents of Russian origin.<sup about="#mwt348" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-107" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-107"}}'><a href="#cite_note-107" id="mwAlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlg">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwAlo" aria-labelledby="Alleged_Russian_connections"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Alleged_Russian_connections">Alleged Russian connections</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Alleged Russian connections"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwAls">Following Revolut's incorporation in Lithuania, the company faced allegations of ties to the Russian authorities. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stasys_Jakeliūnas" title="Stasys Jakeliūnas" id="mwAlw">Stasys Jakeliūnas</a>, who served as the head of the Lithuanian parliament’s budget and finance committee, stated concerns that the father of Revolut's CEO Storonsky was a top manager of a state-owned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gazprom" title="Gazprom" id="mwAl0">Gazprom</a> and that one company's shareholders <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DST_Global" title="DST Global" id="mwAl4">DST Global</a> was connected to Russia via its founder <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuri_Milner" title="Yuri Milner" id="mwAl8">Yuri Milner</a>. Lithuanian media reported that the company's servers may be potentially moved to Russia, further fueling the controversy. The bank initially made a false statement about Storonsky's lack of family connections with Russia, but later confirmed it.<sup about="#mwt351" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-108" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-108" id="mwAmA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmI">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAmQ">In 2022, Storonsky claimed that he opposes the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine" id="mwAmU">Russian invasion of Ukraine</a>. The company offered relocation supports for its Ukraine-based staff.<sup about="#mwt354" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-109" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-109"}}'><a href="#cite_note-109" id="mwAmY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmg">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmk">]</span></span></a></sup> Storonsky renounced his Russian citizenship in October of that year.<sup about="#mwt357" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-110" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-110"}}'><a href="#cite_note-110" id="mwAmo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAms"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmw">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwAm4" aria-labelledby="Automated_suspension_of_accounts_(2020)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Automated_suspension_of_accounts_(2020)"><span id="Automated_suspension_of_accounts_.282020.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Automated suspension of accounts (2020)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: Automated suspension of accounts (2020)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAm8">Revolut, like traditional financial institutions, uses algorithms to identify <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Money_laundering" title="Money laundering" id="mwAnA">money laundering</a>, fraud, and other criminal activity. Under certain anti–money laundering legislation, if suspicious activities are being investigated, bank staff are not allowed to tell customers why their accounts have been frozen.<sup about="#mwt360" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-111" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-111"}}'><a href="#cite_note-111" id="mwAnE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnM">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAnU">It has been reported since 2020 that Revolut's algorithms suspended accounts for weeks or months at a time after unusual activity was detected.<sup about="#mwt361" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CC_112-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CC"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CC-112" id="mwAnY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAng">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt362" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FW_113-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"FW"}}'><a href="#cite_note-FW-113" id="mwAno"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAns"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn0">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut's policies require customers whose accounts were suspended to request a resolution via in-app <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chat_support" title="Chat support" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAn4">chat support</a>.<sup about="#mwt365" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-zdnet_20190117_114-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"zdnet_20190117"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-zdnet_20190117-114"}}'><a href="#cite_note-zdnet_20190117-114" id="mwAn8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoE">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt368" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FW_113-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"FW"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FW-113"}}'><a href="#cite_note-FW-113" id="mwAoM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoU">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt371" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CC_112-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CC"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CC-112"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CC-112" id="mwAoc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAog"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAok">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoo">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut said that "the system is programmed to temporarily lock an account and place it in a queue, until one of our compliance agents can review the case".<sup about="#mwt374" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-115" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-115"}}'><a href="#cite_note-115" id="mwAos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo0">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAo8">In February 2020, <i id="mwApA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Daily_Telegraph" title="The Daily Telegraph" id="mwApE">The Daily Telegraph</a></i> reported that Revolut suspended an account containing £90,000 for more than two months<sup about="#mwt377" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-telegraph_20000125_116-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"telegraph_20000125"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-telegraph_20000125-116"}}'><a href="#cite_note-telegraph_20000125-116" id="mwApI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApQ">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApU">]</span></span></a></sup> and that another customer travelled 500 miles from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auvergne" title="Auvergne" id="mwApY">Auvergne</a> in France to Revolut's London offices in an unsuccessful attempt to recover £15,000 in an account that Revolut had frozen with no justification given.<sup about="#mwt380" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EU_117-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EU"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-EU-117"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EU-117" id="mwApc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApk">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApo">]</span></span></a></sup> The account was later closed and the money in it returned to the customer's other bank accounts.<sup about="#mwt381" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EU_117-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EU"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EU-117" id="mwAps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp0">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAp8">Also in February 2020, <i id="mwAqA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Times" title="The Times" id="mwAqE">The Times</a></i> reported that Revolut suspended and later closed a business account containing €300,000 belonging to Priorité Energie, an energy transition start-up company, preventing the company from paying its staff.<sup about="#mwt384" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NS_118-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NS"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NS-118"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NS-118" id="mwAqI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqQ">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqU">]</span></span></a></sup> Revolut publicly apologised and eventually rectified the problem.<sup about="#mwt385" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NS_118-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NS"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NS-118" id="mwAqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqg">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwAqo" aria-labelledby="UK_fraud_victims"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="UK_fraud_victims">UK fraud victims</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section: UK fraud victims"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAqs">In 2023, Revolut reported a 35% reduction in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authorised_push_payment_fraud" title="Authorised push payment fraud" id="mwAqw">authorised push payment fraud</a>.<sup about="#mwt388" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-119" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-119"}}'><a href="#cite_note-119" id="mwAq0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq8">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the company remained one of the most frequently named financial institutions in UK fraud complaints, prompting scrutiny of its security measures.<sup about="#mwt391" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-120" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-120" id="mwArE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArM">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The number of complaints of fraud reported to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Action_Fraud" title="Action Fraud" class="mw-redirect" id="mwArU">Action Fraud</a>, the UK reporting centre for fraud and cybercrime, by Revolut customers rose from 567 in February 2023 to 1,086 for February 2024.<sup about="#mwt392" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-theguardian_2024apr10_im_98-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"theguardian_2024apr10_im"}}'><a href="#cite_note-theguardian_2024apr10_im-98" id="mwArY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArg">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAro">Prior to Revolut having a banking licence, complaints were made by defrauded Revolut customers to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Ombudsman" title="Financial Ombudsman" class="mw-redirect" id="mwArs">Financial Ombudsman</a>, which in some cases required Revolut to reimburse and compensate victims, and remove <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cifas#Fraud_databases" title="Cifas" id="mwArw">fraud markers</a> wrongly placed against the individuals.<sup about="#mwt395" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-org_4189491_121-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"org_4189491"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-org_4189491-121"}}'><a href="#cite_note-org_4189491-121" id="mwAr0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr8">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAsE">Action Fraud received 10,000 reports of fraud naming Revolut in 2023, 2,000 more than <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barclays" title="Barclays" id="mwAsI">Barclays</a>, one of the UK's largest banks, and twice as many as a competitor bank of similar size to Revolut. That year over 3,500 complaints about Revolut were made to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Ombudsman_Service" title="Financial Ombudsman Service" id="mwAsM">ombudsman</a>, more than any other financial institution. Consumer organisation <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Which%3F" title="Which?" id="mwAsQ">Which?</a> did not recommend banking large sums of money with Revolut, saying "They have a track record of not reimbursing people who fall victim to fraud or find themselves in this incredibly difficult situation, [and] of money being taken from accounts even after scam activity has been reported."<sup about="#mwt398" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-fraud_122-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"fraud"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-fraud-122"}}'><a href="#cite_note-fraud-122" id="mwAsU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsc">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwAsk" aria-labelledby="Partnerships"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Partnerships">Partnerships</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section: Partnerships"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAso">In January 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchester_City_W.F.C." title="Manchester City W.F.C." id="mwAss">Manchester City W.F.C.</a> announced Revolut as the training sleeve kit sponsor. This partnership was later extended to include the back-of-shirt sponsors of both the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchester_City_F.C." title="Manchester City F.C." id="mwAsw">men's</a> and women's teams.<sup about="#mwt401" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123"}}'><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwAs0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAs4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs8">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt404" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-124" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124"}}'><a href="#cite_note-124" id="mwAtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtM">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAtU">That same month, Revolut became an official partner of the French rugby club <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stade_Toulousain" title="Stade Toulousain" id="mwAtY">Stade Toulousain</a>.<sup about="#mwt407" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_125-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-125"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-125" id="mwAtc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtk">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAto">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAts">In July 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_in_Formula_One" title="Audi in Formula One" id="mwAtw">Audi F1 Team</a> announced a multi-year deal with Revolut to be the title sponsor of the team, beginning with the 2026 season.<sup about="#mwt410" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126"}}'><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwAt0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAt4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt8">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuA">]</span></span></a></sup> In the same month, Revolut was named the Official Global Banking and FX Partner for the Italian football club Como 1907.<sup about="#mwt411" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_125-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-125" id="mwAuE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuM">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAuU">In March 2026, Revolut became official back of shirt partner of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchester_City_F.C." title="Manchester City F.C." id="mwAuY">Manchester City F.C.</a>, extending the relationship with the club to the men's team. <sup about="#mwt414" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-127" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-127"}}'><a href="#cite_note-127" id="mwAuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuk">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAus">The company also has partnerships in other sports, such as an ongoing agreement with the NBA to serve as an associate partner for the NBA Paris Game.<sup about="#mwt417" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128"}}'><a href="#cite_note-128" id="mwAuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAu0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu4">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAvA">Beyond sports, Revolut announced a strategic partnership with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wizz_Air" title="Wizz Air" id="mwAvE">Wizz Air</a> in March 2025 to integrate Revolut Pay as a primary payment method for the airline.<sup about="#mwt420" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-129" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-129"}}'><a href="#cite_note-129" id="mwAvI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvQ">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvU">]</span></span></a></sup> In November 2025, the company entered a global payments partnership with Booking.com, which integrated Revolut Pay as a checkout option and adopted Revolut Business for its internal operations. The collaboration also allowed users to earn and redeem RevPoints, Revolut's loyalty program, on travel bookings.<sup about="#mwt423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-130" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-130"}}'><a href="#cite_note-130" id="mwAvY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvg">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAvo">On 3 June 2025, Revolut signed a membership agreement with European Payments Initiative (EPI). The agreement includes integration of Wero, mobile-first wallet and instant account-to-account payment solution, into Revolut.<sup about="#mwt426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-131" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-131" id="mwAvs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv0">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwAv8" aria-labelledby="Workplace_policy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Workplace_policy">Workplace policy</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Revolut&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: Workplace policy"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAwA">In June 2026, Revolut announced that graduate employees and interns joining the company in 2027 would be required to work from the office at least three days a week, marking a retreat from its fully remote policy. The company said the change was intended to support in-person collaboration and mentoring but its remote policy would remain unchanged for other employees.<sup about="#mwt429" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwAwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwM">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

